# Code Review: Payment Callback Idempotency Bug

## Root Cause Analysis

The `PaymentCallbackService.onCallback()` method processes payment callbacks without any idempotency protection. Payment providers commonly retry callbacks due to network issues, timeouts, or load balancing. When the same callback arrives multiple times:

1. **Payment entity is overwritten** - `markPaid()` is called again, potentially overwriting values
2. **Duplicate outbox records** - `outboxRepository.insert()` creates a new record each time
3. **Downstream effects** - Duplicate `PAYMENT_PAID` events may trigger double-processing in event consumers

## Smallest Safe Fix

Add an idempotency check using the provider's unique transaction ID before processing.

### Changes Required

**File: `src/main/java/com/example/payment/PaymentRepository.java`**

```java
package com.example.payment;

public interface PaymentRepository {
    Payment requireByOrderId(String orderId);
    void save(Payment payment);

    // NEW: Check if this provider transaction was already processed
    Payment findByProviderTxnId(String providerTxnId);
}
```

**File: `src/main/java/com/example/payment/PaymentCallbackService.java`**

```java
package com.example.payment;

import java.time.Instant;

public class PaymentCallbackService {
    private final PaymentRepository paymentRepository;
    private final OutboxRepository outboxRepository;

    public PaymentCallbackService(
            PaymentRepository paymentRepository,
            OutboxRepository outboxRepository) {
        this.paymentRepository = paymentRepository;
        this.outboxRepository = outboxRepository;
    }

    public void onCallback(PaymentCallback payload) {
        // IDEMPOTENCY CHECK: Skip if this provider transaction was already processed
        Payment existing = paymentRepository.findByProviderTxnId(payload.getProviderTxnId());
        if (existing != null) {
            return; // Already processed - exit early
        }

        Payment payment = paymentRepository.requireByOrderId(payload.getOrderId());
        payment.markPaid(payload.getProviderTxnId(), Instant.parse(payload.getPaidAt()));
        paymentRepository.save(payment);
        outboxRepository.insert("PAYMENT_PAID", payload.getOrderId(), payload.getProviderTxnId());
    }
}
```

## Why This Fix Works

| Aspect | Explanation |
|--------|-------------|
| **Uniqueness** | `providerTxnId` is unique per payment attempt from the provider |
| **Minimal** | Only 2 methods added/modified, no schema changes |
| **Safe** | Uses existing fields, doesn't change business logic |
| **Idempotent** | Repeated calls with same `providerTxnId` produce same result |

## Regression Checks

1. **First callback succeeds**: New `providerTxnId` → payment marked paid, outbox inserted ✓
2. **Retry callback ignored**: Same `providerTxnId` → early return, no duplicate state ✓
